# Check State and Tailor to This Project

- Use read-only checks when they would make the answer accurate: `git status`, `git branch -v`, `git log`, file contents, directory layout, and docs. Check rather than guess.
- Tailor proposals to the current branch, uncommitted changes, whether CI exists, and the project phase. When a status doc matters, read the relevant section of `docs/status/WHERE_WE_ARE.md`.
- When one check answers the question, give that answer.
